Subject: [M150-LTS] Verify Graphite recording insertion before updating
 SharedImage cleared state

Currently, when a SharedImage is uninitialized, we record a clear
command into the Graphite Recorder and immediately mark the SharedImage
as cleared. However, if the Recording containing the clear fails to be
inserted into the Graphite Context for any reason, the clear command
never executes. Since the cleared flag was already updated on the
SharedImage, Chrome never attempts to clear it again on subsequent
accesses, causing uninitialized memory reads.

This CL propagates the recording insertion success (by returning a bool
from FlushGraphiteRecorder and FlushWriteAccess) up to the callsites,
and defers calling SetCleared() / SetClearedRect() until we know the
Graphite recording insertion successfully completes.

(cherry picked from commit 872f3f32bf81dfa4efa23352c1741267401ea14f)

